    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Shiloh (תל שילה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Shiloh (תל שילה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Samaria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.7 (Pages 113)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>A rock-cut and plastered cistern (Cistern 1320) found in the courtyard of an Iron Age I house (Layer V and IV).</p>]]></description>
